              <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>WOSBAB</td>\n                <td>₦1,720.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ZAMSON</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,720.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,720.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>EMADEB</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Oil Flows Under Pressure as Tanker Traffic Falls\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Tanker movements through the Strait of Hormuz have dropped sharply as the US-Iran standoff shows no clear sign of ending. Only five tanker crossings were recorded on Wednesday and nine on Thursday, compared with a monthly average of 12 crossings.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-oil-flows-under-pressure-as-tanker-traffic-falls\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Crisis: 94 Countries Turn to Fuel Subsidies as Nigerians Pay More\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria is facing renewed pressure from the global energy shock. Governments in 94 countries introduce fuel subsidies, price caps and tax measures to shield consumers from soaring energy costs. The International Energy Agency said more than 115 countries had introduced measures in response to the crisis.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-crisis-94-countries-turn-to-fuel-subsidies-as-nigerians-pay-more\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Aradel Targets 2027 for Petrol Production at Ogbele Refinery\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Aradel Holdings Plc plans to begin producing petrol at its Ogbele modular refinery in 2027. The 11,000-barrel-a-day facility in Rivers State currently produces kerosene, diesel, gas oil and naphtha. The company is separately weighing investment in aviation fuel production, which it views as an export opportunity.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/aradel-targets-2027-for-petrol-production-at-ogbele-refinery\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Rise as U.S. Threatens Indefinite Iran Blockage\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude stood at $87.06 per barrel, down marginally by 0.01%, while WTI crude was trading at $81.28 per barrel. Brent and WTI remained on course for weekly gains of about 4%, despite Thursday's decline of more than 2%. The market is being pulled between two competing forces: the threat of prolonged supply disruption in the Middle East and growing concerns over oil demand.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-rise-as-us-threatens-indefinite-iran-blockage\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Crisis Pushes Oil Prices To Tipping Point, $120 Crude in Sight\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The global oil market is showing a widening disconnect between falling crude futures and increasingly tight physical fuel markets. The prolonged disruption to shipping through the Strait of Hormuz continues to erode inventories and restrict supplies. Diesel, gasoil and jet fuel supplies are tightening as refinery disruptions in the Middle East and Russia reduce export availability.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-crisis-pushes-oil-prices-to-tipping-point-120-crude-in-sight\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
